      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Sludge G",
      "description": "Evening at the Bodetal reservoir , Harz, 29 April 1990.N  I think the interesting looking concrete building housed the pumping engines . The Rappbode Talsperre system is described here\nTHe dam is 106 m high and 415 m long completed apparently by the West German firm Polensky &amp; Zöllner from Frankfurt am Main.  The work started on 1 September 1952  (although a start was made between 1938 and 1942 during Nazi times) and was handed over on 3 October 1959. The concrete road on top of the dam was renewed between 2001-3, having previously been cobbled.  The large stone plaques commemorating the building of this dam, to the workers and architects and engineers still exist (see the WIkipedia page) but the DDR Staatswappen of the hammer, compasses and wreath of corn have disappeared.  They looked like this and this in 1990, lining the entrance to the tunnel in this fashion",
      "dateCreated": "1990-04-29",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "rappbode-dam-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "u1pw",
      "smallPath": "_m/u/1/p/w/rappbode-dam-wp/rappbodetalsperre-29-apr-1990--small.webp"
    },
